<title>ITALY: Italy's Milan sees Sept CPI at 4.0 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Italy's Milan sees Sept CPI at 4.0 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Italian city of Milan said its September consumer price index stood at 0.2 percent month-on-month and 4.0 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>In August, Milan's inflation rate was 0.0 percent and 4.0 percent respectively.</p>
<p>Milan is one of 10 Italian cities publishing inflation data on Monday and Tuesday.</p>
<p>The city's CPI has a weighting of 19.1 percent on the national index. The 10 sample cities have a combined weighting of 69.67 percent on the total index.  </p>
<p>Following is the breakdown of the price changes.</p>
<p>(figures in brackets refer to August 1996):</p>
<p>					    Month/Month     Year/Year</p>
<p>    General index		     0.2   (0.0)     4.0  (4.0)</p>
<p>    Food				  0.4  (-0.2)     4.8  (4.5)</p>
<p>    Clothing and footwear	   0.2   (0.0)     4.9  (5.0)</p>
<p>    Housing and utility charges   0.5   (0.3)     9.1  (8.5)</p>
<p>    Furniture			   0.0   (0.0)     3.4  (3.4)</p>
<p>    Health services		   0.2   (0.0)     1.9  (2.1)</p>
<p>    Transportation		   -0.1   (0.2)     4.2  (4.4)</p>
<p>    Entertainment and culture     0.4   (0.4)     2.3  (1.9)</p>
<p>    Education			   0.1   (0.1)    -0.2  (4.7)</p>
<p>    Hotels and restaurants	  0.0   (0.0)     3.8  (4.1)</p>
<p>    Other goods or services	 0.0   (0.0)     2.0  (2.2)</p>
<p>-- Milan newsroom ++392 66129526</p>
